& [VerbatimUserMessage] is the preserved dictation
  + [text] is "and that token ring passed will have things in it like a hash table, pointers to files, descriptions of intention that it's to follow on the commit, and can be reassigned in the inference pass... which makes me wonder about another thing, because I got the sense that language is operating like a motivator to the AI and I wonder how that can be? how is it that the words I say give you impulses to act? is it that focusing on such instructions emits a signal that the inference engine captures and it tries to match that to a pattern of responses that include an understanding to edit files means engage tool use or something... the impulse to act comes from the software implementation to capture that language pattern, not that the language actually engages the impulse to act?"

& [ContextAnchor] is the immediately preceding design formation
  + [user_name] is token-ring pow-wow inference
  + [formation] is one contract-bound inference job whose participant jobs may use one model, several contexts, or different provider connections
  + [terminal_rule] is the contract completes and every participant receives a receipt, or the contract is explicitly broken and abandoned

& [ProvisionalCarrierDistinction] preserves rather than resolves the design seam
  + [immutable_contract_core] may contain contract identity, purpose and intention digest, admitted file-reference manifest root, register schema, membership, dependency graph root, completion predicate, budgets, and authority boundary
  + [register_head_table] maps stable register identities to version, content digest, durable locator, bounded semantic description, producer, and read or write obligations
  + [custody_or_capability_lease] identifies the current participant, allowed register operations, expected versions, sequence, expiry, and next eligible holders
  + [proposal_sidecar] carries candidate writes, evidence, uncertainty, and requested reassignment without changing committed register state
  + [commit_receipt] advances the epoch and binds accepted writes, refused writes, unchanged heads, awakened readers, remaining obligations, and acknowledgements
  + [reassignment] changes custody, attention projection, or pending work through an append-only transition rather than silently changing the identity of the contract
  + [file_pointer_boundary] is a stable repository-relative or governed URI locator plus snapshot and digest, never a process memory address and never an unverified mutable path alone

& [ProvisionalLanguageActionDistinction] is the discussion boundary
  + [language_conditioning] is that input tokens change transformer activations and therefore the probability of continuations such as explanation, planning, a structured tool call, or refusal
  + [learned_action_pattern] is that training associates instruction forms and task states with response forms that include plans, code edits, and typed tool invocations
  + [structured_action_candidate] is model output naming a tool and arguments under the tool schemas and instruction hierarchy visible to inference
  + [host_dispatch] is external software parsing, validating, authorizing, and executing the proposed tool call
  + [feedback_loop] is the host returning observations to context so later inference can revise, continue, prove, stop, or refuse
  + [motivation_nonclaim] is no separate felt impulse, desire signal, or single inspectable motivational register is claimed
  + [causal_distinction] is language genuinely changes the model's computation, while language acquires durable external consequences only through the agent runtime and its granted capabilities

& [CandidateCantorCompilationSeam]
  + preserve attributed language as source
  + derive alternative intention and duty candidates without erasing ambiguity
  + bind stable subjects, file references, register heads, expected versions, capabilities, and completion conditions
  + compile the binding into a bounded participant turn and capability lease
  + let inference propose reads, writes, tool calls, or reassignment
  + validate proposals against authority, schemas, current heads, dependencies, and budgets
  + commit accepted state through one epoch receipt and reproject that receipt to affected participants
  + preserve refusal, abandonment, unresolved readers, and committed-prefix effects explicitly

& [GovernanceBoundary]
  + [canonical_authority] is absent_pending_SJS_reconciliation_with_the_existing_semantic_token_ring
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [effect_authority] is absent
  + [required_reconciliation] is determine whether the user's richer carrier is a new PowWowContract envelope around the existing byte-identical SemanticRoundToken or a signed revision of that protocol
  + [next] is source-to-SJS formation of the Token-Ring Pow-Wow Inference profile and a deterministic provider-free contract fixture when explicitly commissioned
